<%#
  Rendered into the session card body by the dashboard, so a user running
  several sessions at once can tell which image each one is.

  The card otherwise shows only host, times, and session id -- all identical
  across sessions of this app -- and the app title is fixed by manifest.yml,
  so the image is invisible once the launch form is gone.

  ERB binding here is the BatchConnect::Session itself, which is where
  user_context comes from: the launch form values, read back from
  user_defined_context.json in the session's staged directory. Keys are form
  attribute ids, so this must track form.yml's `custom_image`.

  Escaped because user_context holds the raw form input and the markdown
  renderer returns html_safe output. submit.yml.erb's validation happens
  before staging, so nothing exotic should ever land here -- but the escape
  costs nothing and image references never contain characters it touches.
-%>
<%- image = user_context["custom_image"].to_s -%>
<%- unless image.empty? -%>
**Image:** `<%= ERB::Util.html_escape(image) %>`
<%- end -%>
